#14102
The Foyer Of The Temple Of Paphoset~
   The vast width of this chamber is difficult to determine, even in daylight,
and the shadowy reaches of the far walls are not revealed by torches. The air
is thick with dust, making breathing difficult.
   A massive stone head can be seen below, against the opposite wall of the
chamber, partially covered by sand. Most features of the grim countenance are
worn away, but the figure still reflects great power, and the enormous statue
is an awe-inspiring creation, indicative of the advancement of the culture that
created it.
~
