#14110
The Shrine~
   In the center of this semi-circular, domed chamber stands an empty, eight-
foot high pedestal. Atop the pedestal is a circular depression, designed to
hold the base of a statue. Paphoset intended his likeness to be placed here,
where statues of the divinities, like vassals, would bow their heads in homage.
There is a message carved on the front of the pedestal.
~
