#14197
The Atrium~
   The narrow crawlspace suddenly opens up in to this dimly lit atrium. This
room is completely circular, with walls covered in hieroglyphs carved in
bas-relief. The ceiling here is a smooth, unadorned dome, and what little
light there is appears to come from recessed sources above the lip of the
walls, and is reflected faintly by the dome. What is most disturbing about
this place is the complete lack of any signs of life. It is eerily quiet, and
the air seems cooler than that in the rest of the temple. In stark contrast to
the rest of the temple, this room appears to be dust-free. To the north, there
appears to be another chamber whose entrance is covered by a tattered velvet
curtain.
~
